###### Art. 309

(Amended by Laws 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945 and 46-99 of May 20, 1999). Whoever voluntarily inflicts wounds, strikes blows, commits acts of violence or assault, if they result in the victim
(a) an illness or inability to engage in work for more than twenty days, shall be punished with imprisonment of six months to two years, and a fine* of five hundred to five thousand pesos. He or she may also be sentenced to deprivation of the rights mentioned in article 42, for at least one year, and five at most. When the violence described above has produced mutilation, amputation or deprivation of the use of a limb, loss of sight, of an eye, or other disabilities, the penalty of minor imprisonment shall be imposed on the guilty party. If the wounds or blows voluntarily inflicted have caused the death of the victim, the penalty shall be minor imprisonment, even when the intention of the aggressor
(a) was not to cause the death of the victim.

###### Art. 309

1.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). Violence against women constitutes any action or conduct, public or private, by reason of her gender, that causes physical, sexual or psychological harm or suffering to the woman, through the use of physical force or psychological, verbal violence, intimidation or persecution.

###### Art. 309

2.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). Domestic or intrafamily violence constitutes any pattern of conduct through the use of physical force, or psychological, verbal violence, intimidation or persecution, against one or more members of the family or against any person who maintains a cohabitation relationship, against the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant or ex-cohabitant or consensual partner

*  See clarifying note.

, or against the person with whom he or she has procreated a son or daughter to cause physical or psychological harm to his or her person or damage to his or her property, carried out by the father, mother, tutor, guardian, spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant, ex-cohabitant or consensual partner or person under whose authority, protection or care the family is.
Those guilty of the offenses provided for in the two preceding articles shall be punished with a penalty of at least one year of imprisonment, and five at most, and a fine* of five hundred to five thousand pesos and the restitution of the destroyed, damaged and concealed property, if applicable.

###### Art. 309

3.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945 and amended by Law 46-99 of May 20, 1999). Those guilty of violence shall be punished with a penalty of five to ten years of major imprisonment, when one or more of the following facts occur:
a)	Penetration into the house or place where the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant or ex-cohabitant, or consensual partner is sheltered, and committing there the acts constituting violence, when they are separated or a protection order has been issued, ordering the eviction from the residence of the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant, ex-cohabitant or consensual partner;
b)	When serious bodily harm is caused to the person;
c)	When the aggressor carries a weapon in circumstances such that they do not entail the intention to kill or mutilate;
d)	When the violence is exercised in the presence of children and adolescents, all independently of the provisions of articles 126

*  See clarifying note.

to 129, 187 to 191 of the Code for the Protection of Children and Adolescents (Law No. 14-94);
e)	When accompanied by threats of death or destruction of property;
f)	When liberty is restricted for any cause whatsoever;
g)	When the violation is committed after a protection order has been issued in favor of the victim;
h)	If the person, man or woman, is induced, incited or forced to intoxicate himself or herself with alcoholic or intoxicating beverages, or to take drugs with controlled substances or with any means or substance that alters the will of persons.

###### Art. 309

4.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). In all cases provided for in the preceding articles, the court shall issue a protection order in favor of the victim of violence, and may not, in any case, accept mitigating circumstances in favor of the aggressor. The court shall also condemn, in these cases, the aggressor to the restitution of the destroyed, damaged or concealed property.

###### Art. 309

5.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). In all cases provided for in this title, the court shall impose as an accessory penalty on the offenders, mandatory attendance at therapeutic or family counseling programs for a period of not less than six (6) months in a public or private institution. Compliance with this penalty and its results shall be monitored by the court.

###### Art. 309

6.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). The protection order established in article 309-4 is a provision prior to the investigation and trial issued by the court of first instance, which contains one or all of the following sanctions:

a)	Order to refrain from harassing, intimidating or threatening the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant, or ex-cohabitant or consensual partner or from interfering with the provisional or definitive custody or guardianship agreed upon by virtue of law or a court order;
b)	Order of eviction of the aggressor from the residence of the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant, ex-cohabitant or consensual partner;
c)	Prohibition of access to the residence of the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant, ex-cohabitant or consensual partner;
d)	Prohibition of approaching places frequented by the spouse, ex-spouse, cohabitant, ex-cohabitant or consensual partner;
e)	Prohibition to the victim from moving or concealing the common children;
f)	Order of internment of the victim in shelters or refuges in charge of public or private organizations;
g)	Order to provide services, health care and counseling for the entire family in charge of public or private organizations;
h)	Order to submit financial reports on the management of common property of the company, business, commerce or common lucrative activity;
i)	Prohibition to alienate, dispose of, conceal or transfer property belonging to the victim or common property;
j)	Order to replace the destroyed or concealed property;

k)	Order of conservatory measures regarding the possession of common property and the household furnishings of the house where the family resides;
l)	Order to compensate the victim of violence, without prejudice to any civil actions that may be appropriate, for legal expenses, medical treatment, psychiatric counseling and professional guidance, lodging and other similar expenses.

###### Art. 309

7.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). The court that hears and judges the offense shall ratify the protection order, decreasing or increasing, as the case may be, its content, as an accessory penalty. Compliance with the protection order shall be monitored by the court.

###### Art. 310.- (Amended by Laws 224 of June 26, 1984 and 46-99 of May 20, 1999)

If the circumstances of premeditation or ambush concur in the act, the penalty shall be ten to twenty years of major imprisonment, when the death of the victim follows; and if this does not result, the penalty of three to ten years of major imprisonment shall be imposed on the guilty party.

