###### Art. 334.- (Modified by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). Shall be considered a procurer he or she

1st. Who in any manner aids, assists or harbors persons, men or women with a view to pros-

*  See explanatory note.
** See explanatory note.

titution or the recruitment of persons with a view to sexual exploitation;
2nd. He or she who from the exercise of that practice receives benefits from prostitution;
3rd. He who in connection with prostitution cannot justify the resources corresponding to his standard of living;
4th. He or she who consents to the prostitution of his or her partner and obtains benefits from it;
5th. Who hires, trains or maintains, even with his or her consent, a person, man or woman, even of legal age with a view to prostitution, or to debauchery and relaxation of morals;
6th. Who acts as intermediary, in any capacity, between persons (men or women) who engage in prostitution or the relaxation of morals or individuals who exploit or remunerate the prostitution and relaxation of morals of another;
7th. Who by threats, pressure or maneuvers, or by any means, disturbs the action of prevention, assistance or reeducation undertaken by qualified organizations in favor of persons (men or women) who engage in prostitution or are at risk of prostitution.
Procuring is punished with imprisonment from six months to three years and a fine* of fifty thousand to five hundred thousand pesos.
The attempt of the offenses provided for in this article shall be punished with the same penalty as the completed act.

###### Art. 334

1.- (Added by Law 24-97 of January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945 and modified by Law 46-99 of May 20, 1999). The penalty shall be major imprisonment from two to ten

*  See explanatory note.

years and a fine* of one hundred thousand to one million pesos in the following cases:
1st. When the offense has been committed with respect to a child or adolescent of any sex, without prejudice to the provisions of articles 126 to 129, 187 to 191 of the Code for the Protection of Children and Adolescents;
2nd. When the offense has been accompanied by threat, violence, assault, abuse of authority or fraud;
3rd. When the perpetrator of the offense was carrying an apparent or concealed weapon;
4th. When the perpetrator of the offense is the husband, wife, cohabitant, father or mother of the victim or belongs to one of the categories established in article 303-4;
5th. When the perpetrator is vested with public authority or when, by reason of his or her position, he or she is called to participate, by the very nature of his or her functions, in the fight against prostitution, the protection of health or the maintenance of public order;
6th. When the offense has been committed with respect to several persons;
7th. When the victims of the offense have been delivered or incited to engage in prostitution outside the national territory;
8th. When the victims of the offense have been delivered or incited to engage in prostitution upon their arrival abroad or within a short time of their arrival abroad;
9th. When the offense has been committed by several perpetrators, co-perpetrators or accomplices.

*  See explanatory note.

The penalties provided for in article 334 and in this article shall be pronounced even when the various acts that are the constituent elements of the offense have been carried out in different countries.
The attempt of these acts shall be punished with the same penalties as the completed act.
In none of the cases provided for in Paragraph I of Sexual Assaults may mitigating circumstances be accepted in favor of the male or female aggressor.

###### Art. 335

Those guilty of the crime mentioned in the preceding article shall be disqualified from exercising the positions of guardian or curator, and from being part of family councils, for at least one year and at most three, if the guilty party is included in the first paragraph of this article; and if he or she is in the second, the disqualification shall last from one to five years. In addition to the penalties that this article imposes on those who become guilty of crimes against decency, if the guilty party is a first-degree ascendant, legitimate or natural, of the offended party, he or she shall be deprived of the rights and benefits that the Civil Code grants to parents in the treatment of parental authority over the person and property of their children. In all the cases dealt with by the preceding provisions, the guilty parties shall be subject by the sentence of conviction to the special surveillance of the high police, for a time equal to that of the sentence, or to that of the disqualification that is decreed.

###### PARAGRAPH III.- ATTACKS AGAINST THE PERSONALITY AND DIGNITY OF THE PERSON

###### Art. 336.- (Modified by Law No. 24-97 dated January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945)

Constitutes discrimination any distinction made between natural persons by reason of their origin, age, their sex, their family situation, their state of health, their disabilities, their customs, their political opinions, their union activities, their occupation, their belonging or their non-belonging, true

or supposed, to an ethnicity, a nation, a race or a particular religion.
Also constitutes discrimination any distinction made between legal persons by reason of the origin, their age, the sex, family situation, state of health, disabilities, customs, political opinions, union activities, the belonging or non-belonging true or supposed to an ethnicity, a nation, a race, or a particular religion of the members or of any of the members of the legal person.

###### Art. 336

1.- (Added by Law 24-97 dated January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). The discrimination defined in the preceding article committed with respect to a natural or legal person is punished with imprisonment of two years and a fine of fifty thousand pesos, when it consists of:
1st. Refusing the supply of a good or a service;
2nd. Hindering the normal exercise of any economic activity;
3rd. Refusing to hire, sanction or dismiss a person;
4th. Subordinating the supply of a good or service to a condition based on one of the elements provided for in the preceding article;
5th. Subordinating a job offer to a condition based on one of the elements provided for in the preceding article.

###### Art. 337.- (Modified by Law 24-97 dated January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945)

Is punished with imprisonment from six months to one year and a fine* of twenty-five thousand to fifty thousand pesos the act of voluntarily attacking the privacy of private life, he or those persons who by means of any of the following procedures:
1.	Capture, record or transmit, without the consent of their author, words spoken in a private or confidential manner;
2.	Capture, record or transmit, without his or her consent, the image of a person who is in a private place;
When the acts mentioned in this article have been carried out with the knowledge of the interested parties, without their having opposed it, their consent is presumed.

*  See explanatory note.

###### Art. 337

1.- (Added by Law 24-97 dated January 28, 1997 G.O. 9945). Is punished with the same penalty the act of preserving, carrying or allowing to be brought to the knowledge of the public or of a third party, or using, in any manner whatsoever, any recording or document obtained with the aid of one of the acts provided for in the present article.
When the offense provided for in the preceding paragraph is committed by means of the written or audiovisual press, the particular provisions of Law No. 6132 on Expression and Dissemination of Thought, of the year 1962, apply insofar as concerns the determination of the responsible persons.

