translated_text:
###### Art. 471.- Those who commit the following shall be punished with a fine* of one peso

1.- Those who neglect the repair and cleaning of ovens, chimneys, and machines where fire and flame are used;
2.- Those who set off fireworks in a place prohibited by the authority;
3.- Innkeepers and other persons who neglect lighting, when this duty is imposed upon them by municipal regulations;
4.-  (Modified by Law 4381 of February 7, 1956 G.O. 7945). Those who also neglect the cleaning of streets or places of transit, in municipalities where such care is left in charge of the inhabitants;
5.- Those who obstruct a public way, depositing or leaving in it, without necessity, materials or any other things that impede freedom of transit, or diminish its safety;
6.- Those who violate the safety rules relating to the deposit of materials in streets or plazas and to the opening of pits and excavations;
7.- Those who violate the regulations concerning local roads;
8.- Those who throw or deposit in front of their buildings, materials and objects that by their nature may cause harm in their fall, or be harmful by their unhealthy exhalations;

*  See clarifying note.

9.-  Those who in streets, roads, plazas, public places or in the fields, leave machines, instruments or weapons that may be abused by thieves and wrongdoers;
10.- Those who extinguish public lighting, or that of the exterior of portals or staircases of houses;
11.- Those who pick and eat fruits on another's property, provided that no other circumstances foreseen by law are involved in the act;
12.- Those who scandalize with their drunkenness;
13.- Those who go out masked, at a time not permitted, or in a manner contrary to the regulations;
14.- Those who bathe in a public place, violating the rules of decency;
15.- Those who throw dead animals in prohibited sites;
16.- Those who without having been provoked insult some person, except in cases foreseen in the treatment of defamation and insults;
17.- Those who through imprudence throw filth upon one or more persons;
18.- Those who without right enter another's land, sown or prepared for sowing. For the purposes of this provision, those who are not owners, settlers or lessees of the land, or who are not agents or representatives of these, or who do not have the right of passage through the land, are considered without right;
19.- Those who allow their cattle or beasts to graze on another's land, before the crops are harvested;
20.- Those who violate the regulations issued by the administrative authority within the scope of its powers;

21.- Those who do not submit to the regulations and decisions published by the municipal authority, by virtue of the powers given to it by the laws.

###### Art. 472

In the cases foreseen in paragraphs 2 and 9 of this article, the fireworks, machines and instruments mentioned therein shall be subject to confiscation.

###### Art. 473

Arrest of one to three days may be pronounced simultaneously with the fine, in those cases in which according to the circumstances, and in the judgment of the judge hearing the contravention, the guilty parties deserve this penalty.

###### Art. 474

In case of recidivism, and whatever the circumstances may be, the penalty of arrest shall always be imposed on the guilty parties, for a maximum of three days.

SECCIÓN 2DA.: SEGUNDA CLASE

