3.- On those who cause the same damage, as a consequence of the speed or poor direction of the beasts, carriages or carts which they are driving, or of the excessive load placed upon them;
4.-  On those who have caused the same accidents due to the age, deterioration or lack of repair or maintenance of houses or buildings, or due to the destruction or excavation or any other works in or near squares, roads or public thoroughfares, without the customary precautions or signals;
5.-  On those who cause the same damage through clumsiness or lack of necessary precaution in the handling of weapons;
6.-  On those who cause the same damage by throwing stones or other hard objects;
