9.- On pharmacists who dispense medicines of poor quality or substitute some for others;
10.- (Modified by article 27 of Law 3925 of September 16, 1954 G.O. 7761). On those who use in their trade weights or measures different from those established by the laws in force;
11.- (Modified by article 27 of Law 3925 of September 16, 1954 G.O. 7761). On bakers or butchers who sell bread or meat of poor quality, and without having the weight for which they should sell;
12.- On those who for profit interpret dreams, make predictions or divinations; or who in another similar manner abuse credulity;

13.- On those who take part in charivaris or other gatherings offensive to any person, and which disturb the tranquility of the inhabitants;
14.- On those who intentionally remove or tear down posters or notices affixed by order of the authority;
