16.- On those who damage in any manner the public roads, or who usurp part of their width;
17.- (Modified by Law 4381 of February 7, 1956 G.O. 7945). On those who, without being duly authorized, remove from public roads grass, earth or stones, or who in places belonging to the municipalities take clay or materials, unless there exists a general custom that authorizes it.

